00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.150 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  24 hours after the city came together to  celebrate they returned to remember  [Music]  now we will read the names of the five  beautiful souls that were lost yesterday  wilhelm  hospital  virginia sorensen  lyanna owen  this time the authorities were taking no  chances using trucks to block the roads  as thousands gathered for a candlelit  vigil  the chief of police among those paying  their respects  how is waukesha feeling tonight  right now our morning  right and we're going to move forward in  the future and heal this is a very  resilient community and i'm very proud  and honored to be  a member and part of this community  overwhelmed mystified  horrified  and  wondering  how could it happen and now how do we  move forward  this event  shows what waukesha really stands for  and and how the how the people care for  each other  on sunday night the first sign of  trouble was the screams  as a large car tore through the crowd of  families hitting adults and children  again  and again  and again i heard and saw  the people being hit but what you could  do more than seeing is hearing and just  that sound was  insane  those injured including toddlers and  three sets of siblings  neil stolzmark has run the karate studio  here for 40 years  everyone was just crying and screaming  and  i ran out to try to help the  victims  one man 39 year old daryl brooks is in  custody his criminal record stretches  back decades  police want to charge him with five  counts of first-degree intentional  homicide when he appears in court later  today  there are few signs now of the horror  that happened on this street beyond some  police markings on the ground and yet  the pain  the confusion the shock is everywhere in  this small commuter town everyone in  walk ashore seems to know someone who's  been affected  the theme of this year's parade was  comfort and joy  but in the last 24 hours this town has  witnessed trauma and tragedy that it  will never forget  joe pike sky news waukesha wisconsin

